Triage AI – Consolidated Build Reference (Oct 2026)
Owner: Ryan Young, Display & Cell Pros LLC (veteran-owned phone/display repair, Spokane, WA) For: Ryan, building the Triage AI app at triage.displaycellpros.com (repo dcp-triage, PR #1, Vercel) Prepared: Oct 14, 2026. This doc pulls together a read-only search of Ryan's Google Drive and a GitHub code search. No source files were changed. Quoted text is copied from the sources. Anything marked "not read" was found but not opened.
Overview
Triage AI takes in a customer's description of a device problem, sorts the job into a tier, and does one of two things. For routine repairs (Tier 1 and Tier 2) it gives a quote using the V4 pricing formula: part cost × 1.8 + $75 labor, plus a $25 trip fee for mobile jobs. For board-level work (Tier 3) it hands the job to Ryan without a firm quote. On the bench side, the Rev 4 design adds schematic and boardview checking and a Chain-of-Verification (CoVe) step, so the system refuses to answer rather than guess at a pinout. The voice and chat intake runs on an ElevenLabs agent ("Virtual Ryan"). The best existing dashboard code is in the refactored website repo on branch fb. Many sources still use older pricing ($50/hr or $85/hr). Treat those as replaced by V4 (see "Conflicts and gaps").


