1. CAD / schematic checking
Key specs


* Motherboard schematics and boardview files (.brd, .fz, .cad) are converted to SVG. The SVG has separate layers for traces, components, and nets (layer-traces, layer-components, layer-nets).
* Each pad is tagged with its part, pin, and net, for example data-ref="U7100" data-pin="24" data-net="PPBUS_G3H".
* Diode-mode readings are colored by how far they drift from the expected value:
   * Green (normal): ΔV_rel ≤ 0.05
   * Amber (drift/degraded): 0.05 < ΔV_rel ≤ 0.15
   * Red (short to ground or open circuit): ΔV_rel > 0.15, or V_meas ≤ 0.005 V
* Every net name the system shows must exist in the active board's verified netlist database.
* Before checking, the system asks the technician to confirm the board revision from the physical 820-series PCB silk-screen number.
* If retrieval fails, the system falls back to deterministic diode-mode lookup tables stored in Vercel KV.
* Netlists are split up by functional block, with 15% overlap at the boundary nodes. Fault-injection simulation runs a breadth-first search (BFS) over the netlist graph.


